  "notes": [
    "Variant nodes and variant-derived association edges are scoped to Homo sapiens (NCBITaxon:9606).",
    "ClinVar rows are filtered to configured human primary chromosomes and assemblies before cleaned outputs are written.",
    "ClinVar variation-level records are not automatically equivalent to GWAS dbSNP/risk-allele records.",
    "Variant-to-variant overlap edges expose shared dbSNP identifiers, scope warnings, and potential selected-node conflicts without forcing unsafe exact merges.",
    "UniProt natural variant features are protein-level annotations and should be interpreted as consequence/context evidence unless identifiers support stronger equivalence.",
    "Disease, gene, and protein association targets are resolved to existing IFX harmonizer IDs when an unambiguous disease/target crosswalk exists; raw source IDs are retained on each edge as provenance.",
    "Unmapped or ambiguous disease/trait assertions remain source CURIEs and are explicitly flagged in target_mapping_status."
  ]
